  "raw": " London on May 7 and the verdict was given the following day after a return.\n\nLast week, he was reportedly hospitalised after contracting an infection likely just as a result of being sleeping in a wet, mosquito-infested bed, according to a report by a senior Nigerian health source.\n\nOritsefemi Owolewa, Nigerian health minister for 10 years, said: “President Buhari is doing great. He spent four night in London but his health has improved. He continued travelling across the country, chaperoned by his sons and senatorial aides.”\n\nAs news of the verdict began to circulate, supporters of Buhari wept as they faced a lack of data backing up their claims that the verdict was “fake news.”\n\nMany of them preferred to meet privately rather than make their cause their cause for public opinion, aside from the #IStandWithMuhammad hashtag and the #ReleaseOurMalam trending on",
